trol flows (recurring tool-call sequences) and predictable data dependencies (parameter passing between tools). By exploiting these properties, PASTE improves agent serving performance through speculative tool execution. Experimental results against state of the art baselines show that PASTE reduces average task completion time by 48.5% and improves tool execution throughput by 1.8 × \times . † † copyright: none † † journalyear: 2026 1. Introduction Figure 1 . Example patterns observed in execut

